<speak version="1.0" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2001/10/synthesis" xmlns:mstts="https://www.w3.org/2001/mstts" xml:lang="en-US"><voice name="en-US-EmmaMultilingualNeural">Number seventeen.<break time="1150ms"/></voice><voice name="en-US-AndrewMultilingualNeural">The Riverside Science Center will open its space exhibition this Saturday. The main hall will be available from nine, but the planetarium will remain closed until one because new equipment is being tested. Visitors with morning planetarium tickets may use them for any afternoon show. The cafe and gift shop will operate on their normal schedule.<break time="1300ms"/></voice><voice name="en-US-EmmaMultilingualNeural">Question.<break time="350ms"/></voice><voice name="en-US-EmmaMultilingualNeural">What can morning planetarium ticket holders do?</voice></speak>
